{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And you shall remember all the way</b> — He says: you will be able to know that there is complete good in the performance of the commandments, and the righteous will not be forsaken nor seek bread, for HaShem sustains you in the wilderness through a great miracle because you walk after His commandments. And I have already explained in the section of the manna (Exodus 16:4) the meaning of <span class=\"he\">לְמַעַן עַנֹּתְךָ לְנַסֹּתְךָ לָדַעַת אֶת אֲשֶׁר בִּלְבָבְךָ הֲתִשְׁמֹר מִצְוֹתָיו אִם לֹא</span> (in order to afflict you, to test you, to know what is in your heart, whether you will keep His commandments or not): that the trial was great for them, for they had no stratagem for themselves, and they entered the great wilderness — not a place of bread — and they had nothing at all apart from the manna; rather, it came down day by day, and the heat of the sun melted it, and they hungered for it greatly. And all this they did to keep the commandment of HaShem, to walk as He would command. And HaShem could have led them on the road of the cities around them, but He brought them into this trial, for from it it would be known that they would keep His commandments forever."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:14:01.452955350Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}